WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.197
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.197 --> 00:00:07.422
<v Examiner>Identify the two long-term goals of the New Zealand Health Strategy 2023,

3
00:00:07.422 --> 00:00:12.503
<v Examiner>and describe how one of its priority areas applies to nursing practice.

4
00:00:12.953 --> 00:00:17.667
The strategy is published under the Pae Ora, Healthy Futures, Act 2022,

5
00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:20.522
and its vision is pae ora, healthy futures:

6
00:00:20.522 --> 00:00:24.307
a future where people from every community can live well,

7
00:00:24.307 --> 00:00:27.892
and where communities and environments support health.

8
00:00:27.892 --> 00:00:31.279
It sets a direction for the next five to ten years.

9
00:00:31.729 --> 00:00:33.285
Its two long-term goals.

10
00:00:33.285 --> 00:00:37.758
One: to achieve health equity, especially for Māori, Pacific peoples,

11
00:00:37.758 --> 00:00:42.167
disabled people and other groups who currently have poorer outcomes.

12
00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:47.613
Two: to improve health outcomes for all New Zealanders, so everyone can live longer,

13
00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:50.011
healthier and more independent lives.

14
00:00:50.461 --> 00:00:52.630
Its six priority areas, in order.

15
00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.799
Voice at the heart of the system.

16
00:00:54.799 --> 00:00:56.573
Flexible, appropriate care.

17
00:00:56.573 --> 00:00:58.019
Valuing our workforce.

18
00:00:58.019 --> 00:00:59.268
A learning culture.

19
00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:01.568
A resilient and sustainable system.

20
00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:04.328
And partnerships for health and wellbeing.

21
00:01:04.778 --> 00:01:05.826
Now describe one.

22
00:01:05.826 --> 00:01:08.845
Take the first, voice at the heart of the system:

23
00:01:08.845 --> 00:01:14.268
recognising and responding to the voices of people and communities throughout the health

24
00:01:14.268 --> 00:01:19.321
system, honouring Te Tiriti, and adapting to diverse and under-served communities.

25
00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:24.560
In nursing practice that means the person and their whānau shape their own care plan.

26
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.257
You ask what matters to them, you involve them in decisions,

27
00:01:28.257 --> 00:01:31.092
and you advocate when their voice isn't heard.

28
00:01:31.092 --> 00:01:33.988
Or take the second, flexible, appropriate care:

29
00:01:33.988 --> 00:01:37.316
preventing illness and delivering care closer to home,

30
00:01:37.316 --> 00:01:39.658
with access for the most under-served.

31
00:01:39.658 --> 00:01:44.403
For a nurse, that's home visits, telehealth, and removing barriers to access.

32
00:01:44.853 --> 00:01:49.794
Health Strategy 2023, under the Pae Ora, Healthy Futures, Act 2022.

33
00:01:49.794 --> 00:01:50.975
Vision: pae ora.

34
00:01:50.975 --> 00:01:56.580
Two goals: health equity, especially for Māori, Pacific and disabled people;

35
00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.645
and better outcomes for all.

36
00:01:58.645 --> 00:02:04.989
Six priorities: voice at the heart; flexible, appropriate care; valuing our workforce;

37
00:02:04.989 --> 00:02:09.045
a learning culture; a resilient and sustainable system;

38
00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:11.848
partnerships for health and wellbeing.
